{"name":"Moonwalk","hex":"#bebec4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Moonwalk","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A barangay of Parañaque, Metro Manila, Philippines."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Moonwalk"}],"entries":[{"title":"Extravehicular activity","blocks":[{"text":"Extravehicular activity (EVA) is any activity performed by an astronaut in outer space outside of a spacecraft. This includes spacewalks, lunar or planetary surface exploration, and stand-up EVAs (SEVAs) where astronauts stand through an open hatch without fully leaving the spacecraft. EVAs have been conducted by the Soviet Union/Russia, the United States, and China, with astronauts from Canada, Japan, the United Arab Emirates, and the European Space Agency also participating in EVAs conducted by those nations. Since there is no atmosphere in space, the astronaut is completely dependent on the space suit for environmental support."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Volkov_during_Russian_EVA28.jpg/330px-Volkov_during_Russian_EVA28.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Extravehicular_activity","wikidata":"Q182020"},{"title":"Lists of spacewalks and moonwalks","blocks":[{"text":"The Lists of spacewalks and moonwalks include:"}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lists_of_spacewalks_and_moonwalks","wikidata":"Q450077"},{"title":"Moonwalk (dance)","blocks":[{"text":"The moonwalk, or backslide, is a popping dance move in which the performer glides backwards but their body actions suggest forward motion. It became popular around the world when American singer Michael Jackson performed the move during the performance of \"Billie Jean\" on Motown 25: Yesterday, Today, Forever, which was broadcast in 1983; he later incorporated it in tours and live performances. Jackson has been credited as renaming the \"backslide\" as the moonwalk and it became his signature move. The moonwalk existed for decades before it had that name: Cab Calloway called it \"the buzz\"; California's black dancers called it the backslide; tap dancers, a skate; and the French mime artist Marcel Marceau called it \"walking against the wind.\""}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Moonwalk_paso.gif/330px-Moonwalk_paso.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moonwalk_(dance)","wikidata":"Q204050"},{"title":"Moonwalk (book)","blocks":[{"text":"Moonwalk is a 1988 autobiography by American singer Michael Jackson. It was first published by Doubleday on February 1, 1988, five months after the release of Jackson's album Bad in 1987, and was named after Jackson's signature dance move, the moonwalk. The book was edited and contains a foreword by Jacqueline Kennedy Onassis, who was the first lady of the United States from 1961 to 1963."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/16/Moonwalk_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moonwalk_(book)","wikidata":"Q2457954"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Sts114_033.jpg/500px-Sts114_033.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Sts114_033.jpg/1280px-Sts114_033.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Sts114_033.jpg/500px-Sts114_033.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Stephen Robinson riding the Canadarm2 while conducting the first in-flight repair of the Space Shuttle during STS-114 on August 3, 2005. The landmass in the backdrop is the Bari region of Somalia.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASts114_033.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/EdWhiteFirstAmericanSpacewalker.1965.ws.jpg/500px-EdWhiteFirstAmericanSpacewalker.1965.ws.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/EdWhiteFirstAmericanSpacewalker.1965.ws.jpg/1280px-EdWhiteFirstAmericanSpacewalker.1965.ws.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/EdWhiteFirstAmericanSpacewalker.1965.ws.jpg/500px-EdWhiteFirstAmericanSpacewalker.1965.ws.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ed White performs the first American spacewalk during Gemini IV.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEdWhiteFirstAmericanSpacewalker.1965.ws.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/A_Man_on_the_Moon%2C_AS11-40-5903_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-A_Man_on_the_Moon%2C_AS11-40-5903_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/A_Man_on_the_Moon%2C_AS11-40-5903_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-A_Man_on_the_Moon%2C_AS11-40-5903_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/A_Man_on_the_Moon%2C_AS11-40-5903_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-A_Man_on_the_Moon%2C_AS11-40-5903_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Buzz Aldrin walks on the Moon during the pioneering Apollo 11 mission in 1969.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_Man_on_the_Moon%2C_AS11-40-5903_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Shenzhou-15_spacewalk.jpg/500px-Shenzhou-15_spacewalk.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.